```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    String city = owner.getCity();
    String city3 = city.substring(0, Math.min(3, city.length())).toUpperCase();
    String lastName = owner.getLastName();
    String last3 = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase();
    long sequence = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
        .filter(existing -> city.equals(existing.getCity()))
        .count() + 1;
    owner.setCustomerCode(String.format("%s-%s-%04d", city3, last3, sequence));
}
```

### Storage: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`
Field `private String customerCode;` mapped to column `customer_code` (lines 60-61), with getter/setter (lines 133-139). Also relevant Owner fields: `city`, `telephone` (E.164 `@Pattern` `^\+[0-9]{8,15}$`), `email`, `postcode`, `registrationDate`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `householdMemberCount`, and `hasEmail()` helper (lines 121-123).

### Consumers of customerCode:
- `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` (below) — derives `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` from it.
- `AuditOwnerCreated` — logs it.
- `openapi.yml` line 2092-2097 (DTO schema, stale description `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`).

---

## 2. Membership number & check digit (derived from customerCode)

### Check digit: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/CustomerCode.java`
Luhn check digit over the digits in the code (non-digits ignored). Single source of truth for the `checkDigit` response field.
```java
public static int checkDigit(String code) {
    int sum = 0;
    boolean dbl = true;
    for (int i = code.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        char c = code.charAt(i);
        if (c < '0' || c > '9') {
            continue;
        }
        int d = c - '0';
        if (dbl) {
            d *= 2;
            if (d > 9) {
                d -= 9;
            }
        }
        sum += d;
        dbl = !dbl;
    }
    return (10 - (sum % 10)) % 10;
}
```

### Membership number: computed inline in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`
Line 24, format `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY = last 2 digits of registration year):
```java
@Mapping(target = "membershipNumber", expression = "java(owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100))")
```
Line 23 wires the check digit: `@Mapping(target = "checkDigit", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.CustomerCode.checkDigit(owner.getCustomerCode()))")`.

### Membership LEVEL (separate numeric concept): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/MembershipLevel.java`
Starts at 1, +1 for email, +1 if `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at MAX=3.
```java
public static final int MAX = 3;
public static int of(Owner owner) {
    int level = 1;
    if (owner.hasEmail()) {
        level++;
    }
    if (owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0) {
        level++;
