## 6. normalizedTelephone, telephone normalization, lastName, hashing (SHA-256)

### Telephone normalization: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/OwnerTelephone.java`
`toE164(String)` strips spaces/dashes/brackets, assumes `+61` when no `+`, drops a single leading `0`, requires 8-15 digits, and checks national length (+61→9, +1→10). Full method:
```java
public static String toE164(String value) {
    if (value == null) {
        return null;
    }
    // Strip spaces, dashes and brackets (round and square).
    String cleaned = value.replaceAll("[\\s()\\[\\]-]", "");
    String digits;
    if (cleaned.startsWith("+")) {
        digits = cleaned.substring(1);
    }
    else {
        String national = cleaned.startsWith("0") ? cleaned.substring(1) : cleaned;
        digits = "61" + national;
    }
    if (!digits.matches("[0-9]{8,15}")) {
        return null;
    }
    if (!nationalLengthValid(digits)) {
        return null;
    }
    return "+" + digits;
}
```

